{
  "name": "What's Involved in a Kitchen Countertop Replacement?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Replacing your kitchen countertops might sound like a huge undertaking, but when you break it down, it’s a pretty systematic process. First things first, we'll carefully remove your old countertop. This is where things can get a bit dusty, but don't worry, we're careful about controlling the mess! Once the old surface is gone, we'll thoroughly check your base cabinets. It's super important to make sure they're strong, level, and in good condition to support your new countertop. If they need reinforcement or repair, we'll address that. Next, we'll take precise new measurements – even if we just removed an old one, you always want fresh numbers for the perfect fit. Your new countertop then gets fabricated off-site according to those specs. On installation day, we’ll bring in the new piece, secure it, and carefully reconnect any sink or faucet components. We'll do thorough checks for tight seams, proper sink cutouts, and make sure there are no leaks. While the on-site installation usually takes about a day, the whole process from measurement to fabrication can take several days or more, depending on the material and complexity. We'll keep you in the loop every step of the way, making sure your kitchen transformation is smooth and stress-free for our Colorado clients.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
